<title>ITALY: Olivetti shares seen strongly up at start.</title>
<headline>Olivetti shares seen strongly up at start.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian information technology group Olivetti were expected to open around seven percent higher according to quotations given in pre-bourse trade.</p>
<p>Stocks in Olivetti, which on Monday announced it was selling its troublesome personal computers activities to a newly formed company Piedmont International, were quoted at around 705 lire per ordinary share in pre-bourse activity.</p>
<p>The stock had been suspended at 663.9 lire in early trade on Monday pending the PC announcement which came after trading finished.</p>
<p>-- Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
